            searchBoton: 'Start now',

            // ===== TOP 10 =====
            top10Titulo: 'Top 10 Most Visited Places',
            saberMas: 'Learn more',
            topTituloObelisco: 'Obelisk and Colón Theater',
            topObelisco: 'Admire the iconic Obelisk of Buenos Aires and enjoy the culture of the Colón Theater.',
            topTituloCanalPanama: 'Panama Canal',
            topCanalPanama: 'Admire one of the most impressive engineering works in the world, connecting two oceans.',
            topTituloCristo: 'Christ the Redeemer',
            topCristo: 'Live an unforgettable experience visiting one of the most famous statues in the world.',
            topTituloTorresPaine: 'Torres del Paine',
            topTorresPaine: 'Discover mountains and stunning landscapes in southern Chile.',
            topTituloCartagena: 'Cartagena',
            topCartagena: 'Walk through streets full of history and colonial architecture.',
            topTituloIguazu: 'Iguazu Falls',
            topIguazu: 'One of the most spectacular natural wonders in South America, between Argentina and Brazil.',
            topTituloMachuPicchu: 'Machu Picchu',
            topMachuPicchu: 'Discover the majesty of the ancient Inca city surrounded by mountains and impressive landscapes. Live a unique experience full of history and culture.',
            topTituloTikal: 'Tikal',
            topTikal: 'The majestic Mayan city lost in the Guatemalan jungle, a World Heritage Site.',
            topTituloChichen: 'Chichén Itzá',
            topChichen: 'Admire one of the most impressive Mayan cities, famous for its pyramid and its incredible archaeological legacy.',
            topTituloGalapagos: 'Galápagos Islands',
            topGalapagos: 'A unique natural paradise in Ecuador, home to species found nowhere else on Earth.',

            topDescObelisco: 'The Obelisk is the main symbol of Buenos Aires, located at the intersection of 9 de Julio and Corrientes avenues. The Colón Theater is one of the most important opera houses in the world, with exceptional acoustics and majestic architecture. This package includes a guided tour of both monuments, including theater entry and a tour of the city surroundings.',
            topDescCanalPanama: 'The Panama Canal is an engineering marvel connecting the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans, opened in 1914. Its locks lift ships over the isthmus mountains on an 82-kilometer journey. The Miraflores Visitor Center lets you watch vessels pass up close and learn the history of this wonder that transformed world trade.',
            topDescCristo: 'Christ the Redeemer is a 30-meter statue that crowns Corcovado hill in Rio de Janeiro. It is one of Brazil\'s most recognizable symbols and of Christianity. The trip includes the train ascent to the top, where you can enjoy a spectacular view of the city and Guanabara Bay.',
            topDescTorresPaine: 'Torres del Paine National Park is a paradise for trekking and nature lovers. Its imposing granite peaks, glaciers, turquoise lakes, and native wildlife (guanacos, condors) make it a unique destination in Chilean Patagonia. The package includes guided excursions and accommodation in the park.',
            topDescCartagena: 'Cartagena de Indias is a colonial jewel on the Caribbean coast of Colombia. Its walls, cobblestone streets, plazas, and colorful houses transport you to the past. The city offers a mix of history, culture, gastronomy, and nearby beaches. The tour includes a visit to San Felipe Castle, the historic center, and a chiva ride.',
            topDescIguazu: 'Iguazu Falls, on the border between Argentina and Brazil, is the largest waterfall system in the world with 275 falls plunging from the subtropical rainforest. The Devil\'s Throat, its most imposing drop, shakes the ground with its roar. Declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site, it receives over 1.5 million visitors a year.',
            topDescMachuPicchu: 'Machu Picchu is one of the wonders of the world and the most impressive legacy of the Inca Empire. Located atop a mountain in Peru, this historic sanctuary offers breathtaking views and architecture in perfect harmony with the environment. The trip includes the train from Cusco, entry to the citadel, and a specialized guide.',
            topDescTikal: 'Tikal was one of the most powerful cities of the Mayan civilization, hidden in the Petén jungle of Guatemala. Its temples, such as the Temple of the Great Jaguar, rise above the forest canopy and were featured in a Star Wars film. It receives about 1.2 million visitors a year and has been a World Heritage Site since 1979.',
            topDescChichen: 'Chichén Itzá is the most famous Mayan city on the Yucatán peninsula. Its Kukulcán pyramid is a marvel of astronomy and architecture. The tour includes the Sacred Cenote, the Ball Game, and the Observatory. You will learn about Mayan culture with an expert guide and enjoy local gastronomy.',
            topDescGalapagos: 'The Galápagos Islands, in Ecuador\'s Pacific Ocean, inspired Charles Darwin\'s theory of evolution. Its giant tortoises, marine iguanas, and blue-footed boobies exist nowhere else on the planet. This volcanic archipelago is a World Heritage Site and Marine Reserve, receiving more than 270,000 visitors a year.',

            topFactsObelisco: 'Location: Buenos Aires, Argentina|Height: 67 meters|Year: 1936|Visitors: 2 million/year',
            topFactsCanalPanama: 'Location: Panama City|Opened: 1914|Length: 82 km|Locks: Miraflores and Gatún',
            topFactsCristo: 'Location: Rio de Janeiro, Brazil|Height: 38 meters|Year: 1931|Visitors: 2 million/year',
            topFactsTorresPaine: 'Location: Patagonia, Chile|Area: 242,000 ha|Year: 1959|Visitors: 250k/year',
            topFactsCartagena: 'Location: Cartagena, Colombia|Founded: 1533|Heritage: UNESCO|Visitors: 1.5 million/year',
            topFactsIguazu: 'Location: Argentina and Brazil|Falls: 275|Devil\'s Throat: 80 m|Visitors: 1.5 million/year',
            topFactsMachuPicchu: 'Location: Cusco, Peru|Altitude: 2,430 m|Year: 1450|Visitors: 1.5 million/year',
            topFactsTikal: 'Location: Petén, Guatemala|Heritage: UNESCO 1979|Temple IV: 70 m|Visitors: 1.2 million/year',
            topFactsChichen: 'Location: Yucatán, Mexico|Height: 30 m|Year: 600 AD|Visitors: 2.5 million/year',
            topFactsGalapagos: 'Location: Pacific Ocean, Ecuador|Heritage: UNESCO 1978|Islands: 19|Unique species: 9,000',

