// Quick facts
paisMexico_quickFacts_0_titulo: 'Indigenous multiculturalism',
paisMexico_quickFacts_0_texto: 'Mexico has 68 recognized indigenous peoples, including Nahua, Maya, Zapotec, Mixtec, and Rarámuri. Each maintains its own languages, dress, and traditions. Over 10 million people speak indigenous languages.',
paisMexico_quickFacts_1_titulo: 'Archaeological heritage',
paisMexico_quickFacts_1_texto: 'With over 50,000 registered archaeological sites, Mexico has the largest number of pre-Columbian ruins in the world. Teotihuacán, Chichén Itzá, Palenque, and Monte Albán each housed over 100,000 inhabitants.',
paisMexico_quickFacts_2_titulo: 'Regional economic leader',
paisMexico_quickFacts_2_texto: 'Mexico is the 12th largest economy in the world (nominal GDP: $2.1 trillion USD) and the largest in Latin America in trade with the US. It is a member of the OECD, G20, and USMCA.',
paisMexico_quickFacts_3_titulo: 'UNESCO Gastronomy',
paisMexico_quickFacts_3_texto: 'Traditional Mexican cuisine was declared Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity in 2010. It includes corn, chili, avocado, cacao, and techniques like nixtamalization.',

// Destinations
paisMexico_destinos_chichen_nombre: 'Chichén Itzá',
paisMexico_destinos_chichen_tag: 'Archaeology · Modern Wonder of the World',
paisMexico_destinos_chichen_descripcion: 'Mayan city with the Temple of Kukulcán (El Castillo), one of the 7 wonders of the modern world. A ceremonial center reflecting the advanced Mayan astronomical knowledge.',
paisMexico_destinos_chichen_detalle: 'Built around 600 AD, declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1988. The Temple of Kukulcán has 365 steps, one for each day of the year. During the equinoxes, a serpent of light descends the pyramid.',
paisMexico_destinos_chichen_consejo: 'Visit early to avoid heat and crowds',

paisMexico_destinos_teotihuacan_nombre: 'Teotihuacán',
paisMexico_destinos_teotihuacan_tag: 'Archaeology · City of the Gods',
paisMexico_destinos_teotihuacan_descripcion: 'Pre-Columbian city with the Pyramid of the Sun and the Pyramid of the Moon. One of the largest and most populous cities in the ancient world.',
paisMexico_destinos_teotihuacan_detalle: 'Inhabited since 200 BC, it reached a population of 150,000. The Pyramid of the Sun is 65 meters tall. The Avenue of the Dead extends for 2 km.',
paisMexico_destinos_teotihuacan_consejo: 'Arrive before 9 AM for the best photographic light',

paisMexico_destinos_cancun_nombre: 'Cancún',
paisMexico_destinos_cancun_tag: 'Beach · Caribbean · Luxury',
paisMexico_destinos_cancun_descripcion: 'White-sand beaches and turquoise waters in the Mexican Caribbean. The country\'s most important tourist destination with world-class resorts.',
paisMexico_destinos_cancun_detalle: 'Tourist development began in 1970. The Hotel Zone extends 22 km in the shape of a \'7\'. It has over 100 hotels and free public beaches.',
paisMexico_destinos_cancun_consejo: 'Use public transport to avoid traffic and high taxi costs',

paisMexico_destinos_coyoacan_nombre: 'Coyoacán',
paisMexico_destinos_coyoacan_tag: 'History · Colonial neighborhood · Art',
paisMexico_destinos_coyoacan_descripcion: 'Bohemian and colonial neighborhood in the south of Mexico City. Home to Frida Kahlo, museums, artisan markets, and historic plazas.',
paisMexico_destinos_coyoacan_detalle: 'Former residence of Leon Trotsky. Frida Kahlo\'s Blue House attracts thousands of visitors. Coyoacán\'s center preserves its 16th-century viceregal architecture.',
paisMexico_destinos_coyoacan_consejo: 'Buy online tickets for Casa Azul in advance',

paisMexico_destinos_angel_nombre: 'Monument to Independence',
paisMexico_destinos_angel_tag: 'History · Patriotic symbol',
paisMexico_destinos_angel_descripcion: '36-meter monument on Paseo de la Reforma, the symbolic heart of Mexico City. Known as \'El Ángel\'.',
paisMexico_destinos_angel_detalle: 'Built in 1910 by Porfirio Díaz for the centenary of independence. The golden bronze Winged Victory weighs 7 tons. The crypts contain the remains of national heroes.',
paisMexico_destinos_angel_consejo: 'Visit at night to see the monumental lighting',

paisMexico_destinos_sumidero_nombre: 'Sumidero National Park',
paisMexico_destinos_sumidero_tag: 'Nature · Canyon · Chiapas',
paisMexico_destinos_sumidero_descripcion: 'Spectacular 1,000-meter-deep canyon formed by the Grijalva River. Vertical walls that harbor crocodiles, spider monkeys, and birds.',
paisMexico_destinos_sumidero_detalle: 'The canyon is 35 km long. The Grijalva River is Mexico\'s fifth largest river. The walls reach heights of up to 1,000 meters above the river.',
paisMexico_destinos_sumidero_consejo: 'Take a boat from Chiapa de Corzo early',

paisMexico_destinos_holbox_nombre: 'Holbox Island',
paisMexico_destinos_holbox_tag: 'Beach · Caribbean · Car-free',
paisMexico_destinos_holbox_descripcion: 'Paradise island with no paved streets or cars. 12 km of beaches with crystal-clear waters, flamingos, and whale sharks.',
paisMexico_destinos_holbox_detalle: 'Part of the Yum Balam Biosphere Reserve. Whale shark season: June-September. Punta Cocos offers a virgin beach with flamingos.',
paisMexico_destinos_holbox_consejo: 'Travel in the low season (May-October) for fewer crowds',

paisMexico_destinos_sierragorda_nombre: 'Sierra Gorda de Querétaro',
paisMexico_destinos_sierragorda_tag: 'Nature · UNESCO · Missions',
paisMexico_destinos_sierragorda_descripcion: 'Mountain ecosystem with exceptional biodiversity and 5 18th-century Jesuit missions declared UNESCO Heritage.',
paisMexico_destinos_sierragorda_detalle: 'The 5 missions were built by Junípero Serra between 1750-1760. The area protects over 2,000 plant species and 500 animals, including jaguars.',
paisMexico_destinos_sierragorda_consejo: 'Hire a local guide for safe trekking',

// Culture
paisMexico_cultura_titulo: 'Mexican Culture',
paisMexico_cultura_descripcion: 'Mexico is a unique blend of indigenous (Maya, Nahua, Zapotec) and Spanish heritage, with African and Asian influences. This fusion produced the mestizo culture that defines the country.',
paisMexico_cultura_stats_0_label: 'Recognized indigenous peoples',
paisMexico_cultura_stats_1_label: 'UNESCO World Heritage Sites',
paisMexico_cultura_stats_2_label: 'Years of civilizational history',
paisMexico_cultura_stats_3_label: 'Archaeological sites',

paisMexico_cultura_items_diademuertos_nombre: 'Day of the Dead',
paisMexico_cultura_items_diademuertos_tag: 'Festivity · UNESCO · Oct 31-Nov 2',
paisMexico_cultura_items_diademuertos_descripcion: 'Unique celebration honoring the deceased with altars, sugar skulls, marigolds, and bread of the dead.',
paisMexico_cultura_items_diademuertos_detalle: 'Of pre-Hispanic origin mixed with Catholicism. Traditional offerings have 7 levels representing the path to Mictlán. Declared Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity by UNESCO in 2008.',

paisMexico_cultura_items_barro_nombre: 'Oaxacan Folk Art',
paisMexico_cultura_items_barro_tag: 'Craftsmanship · Black clay',
paisMexico_cultura_items_barro_descripcion: 'Polished black clay figures with metallic shine, created with ancestral techniques over 400 years old.',
paisMexico_cultura_items_barro_detalle: 'Originating from San Bartolo Coyotepec, Oaxaca. The quartz-polishing technique produces the characteristic shine without glazes. Each piece is unique and can take weeks to complete.',

