// History
paisPeru_historia_titulo: 'History of Peru',
paisPeru_historia_descripcion: 'From the first American civilizations to the consolidation of the republic. Peru is the cradle of ancient cultures.',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_0_titulo: 'Caral Civilization',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_0_texto: 'The oldest civilization in the Americas developed in Supe, north of Lima.',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_1_titulo: 'Chavín Culture',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_1_texto: 'Ceremonial center in the Andes. Considered the \'mother culture\' of ancient Peru.',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_2_titulo: 'Expansion of the Inca Empire',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_2_texto: 'Pachacútec begins the expansion of Tahuantinsuyo, which would reach from Colombia to Chile.',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_3_titulo: 'Spanish conquest',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_3_texto: 'Cajamarca: capture of Inca Atahualpa. Beginning of the Viceroyalty of Peru.',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_4_titulo: 'Independence of Peru',
paisPeru_historia_cronologia_4_texto: 'San Martín declares independence in Lima. Consolidated after the Battle of Ayacucho (1824).',

