// Quick facts
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_0_titulo: 'Volcanic landscape',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_0_texto: 'Nicaragua has one of the highest concentrations of volcanoes in Central America, including Concepción Volcano on Ometepe Island and Masaya Volcano with its accessible crater.',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_1_titulo: 'Large lakes',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_1_texto: 'Lake Nicaragua (8,264 km²) is the largest lake in Central America and is home to freshwater sharks. Lake Managua completes the country\'s lacustrine geography.',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_2_titulo: 'Dual coast',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_2_texto: 'Nicaragua has a Pacific coast (San Juan del Sur) and a Caribbean coast (Corn Islands), with very different landscapes, beaches, and cultures (Creole vs indigenous).',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_3_titulo: 'Living tradition',
paisNicaragua_quickFacts_3_texto: 'Music (marimba, son nica), patron saint festivals, and gastronomy (gallo pinto, nacatamales) are central to Nicaraguan daily life.',

// Destinations
paisNicaragua_destinos_granada_nombre: 'Granada',
paisNicaragua_destinos_granada_tag: 'History · Colonial · Founded 1524',
paisNicaragua_destinos_granada_descripcion: 'Very well-preserved colonial city, famous for its architecture and plazas. Founded in 1524. One of the oldest cities in the Americas.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_granada_detalle: 'Granada Cathedral. La Calzada street. La Merced Church (views). Granada Islets (365 islets in Lake Nicaragua). La Polvora Fortress. Malecón.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_granada_consejo: 'Walk the center on foot, in comfortable shoes',

paisNicaragua_destinos_sanjuan_nombre: 'San Juan del Sur',
paisNicaragua_destinos_sanjuan_tag: 'Beach · Surf · Pacific',
paisNicaragua_destinos_sanjuan_descripcion: 'Coastal beach town on the Nicaraguan Pacific. Very popular for sun, sea, and surf tourism. Spectacular sunsets.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_sanjuan_detalle: 'San Juan del Sur Beach (main). Christ of Mercy (panoramic views). Surfing at Maderas, Hermosa, Majagual. Boat tours. Sport fishing.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_sanjuan_consejo: 'Ideal for relaxation and sports',

paisNicaragua_destinos_ometepe_nombre: 'Ometepe Island',
paisNicaragua_destinos_ometepe_tag: 'Volcano · Lake · Adventure',
paisNicaragua_destinos_ometepe_descripcion: 'Volcanic island in Lake Nicaragua, formed by two volcanoes: Concepción (active) and Maderas. Unique natural paradise.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_ometepe_detalle: 'Concepción Volcano (1,610 m, active, challenging trekking). Maderas Volcano (1,394 m, inactive, crater lagoon). Ojo de Agua (natural pools). Petroglyphs. Santo Domingo Beach.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_ometepe_consejo: 'Bring warm clothing and water for trekking',

paisNicaragua_destinos_managua_nombre: 'Managua',
paisNicaragua_destinos_managua_tag: 'Urban · Capital',
paisNicaragua_destinos_managua_descripcion: 'Capital with modern life and history. Political and cultural center. Rebuilt after the 1972 earthquake.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_managua_detalle: 'Old Managua Cathedral (earthquake ruins). New Cathedral. National Palace of Culture. Lake Managua. Salvador Allende Port (malecón). Former Revolution Plaza.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_managua_consejo: 'Visit the historic center and the malecón',

paisNicaragua_destinos_masaya_nombre: 'Masaya Volcano',
paisNicaragua_destinos_masaya_tag: 'Volcano · National parks',
paisNicaragua_destinos_masaya_descripcion: 'Masaya Volcano National Park. Crater accessible by car to the edge. You can see lava and sulfur.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_masaya_detalle: 'Santiago (main crater, emits gas and lava). Viewpoint. Interpretation center. Lava tunnel (volcanic caves). Night tour (nocturnal birds).',
paisNicaragua_destinos_masaya_consejo: 'Bring a mask for sulfur',

paisNicaragua_destinos_leon_nombre: 'León',
paisNicaragua_destinos_leon_tag: 'History · Colonial · University',
paisNicaragua_destinos_leon_descripcion: 'Second most important city in Nicaragua. Colonial historic center. Oldest university in Central America (1813).',
paisNicaragua_destinos_leon_detalle: 'León Cathedral (UNESCO Heritage, largest in Central America, tombs of poets). Ortiz Gurdián Foundation Art Museum. León Viejo Ruins (UNESCO Heritage).',
paisNicaragua_destinos_leon_consejo: 'Climb to the cathedral roof for views',

paisNicaragua_destinos_islasmaiz_nombre: 'Corn Islands',
paisNicaragua_destinos_islasmaiz_tag: 'Caribbean · Snorkeling · Beach',
paisNicaragua_destinos_islasmaiz_descripcion: 'Caribbean archipelago in the Caribbean Sea. Turquoise waters, white sand, and coral reefs.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_islasmaiz_detalle: 'Big Corn Island (tourist development). Little Corn Island (virgin, indigenous community). Diving and snorkeling. Sea turtles. Fried fish and lobster.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_islasmaiz_consejo: 'Book in advance, flight from Managua',

paisNicaragua_destinos_rivas_nombre: 'Rivas',
paisNicaragua_destinos_rivas_tag: 'Nature · Lakes · Volcanoes',
paisNicaragua_destinos_rivas_descripcion: 'Area of lakes and volcanoes in southern Nicaragua. Excellent base for exploring Ometepe Island and San Juan del Sur.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_rivas_detalle: 'Cattle fair. Rivas Church. Nearby beaches and nature. Access to Ometepe. Very good for rural tourism.',
paisNicaragua_destinos_rivas_consejo: 'Excellent base for exploring the southern region',

// Culture
paisNicaragua_cultura_titulo: 'Nicaraguan Culture',
paisNicaragua_cultura_descripcion: 'Nicaraguan culture blends indigenous (Chorotega, Náhuatl), African (Creole on the Caribbean coast), and European influences, with a strong presence in music, festivities, and gastronomy.',
paisNicaragua_cultura_stats_0_label: 'km²',
paisNicaragua_cultura_stats_1_label: 'Large lakes',
paisNicaragua_cultura_stats_2_label: 'Volcanoes',
paisNicaragua_cultura_stats_3_label: 'UNESCO World Heritage Sites',

paisNicaragua_cultura_items_marimba_nombre: 'Nicaraguan Marimba',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_marimba_tag: 'Music · Instrument',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_marimba_descripcion: 'Very important traditional instrument in Nicaragua. Similar to the Guatemalan marimba but with its own style.',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_marimba_detalle: 'Used in patron saint festivals. Son nica is a traditional genre. The marimba is Nicaragua\'s national instrument.',

paisNicaragua_cultura_items_gallopinto_nombre: 'Gallo pinto',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_gallopinto_tag: 'Gastronomy',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_gallopinto_descripcion: 'Very popular typical dish: rice and red or black beans mixed together. Eaten for breakfast, lunch, or dinner.',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_gallopinto_detalle: 'Served with egg, cheese, tortilla, or plantain.',

paisNicaragua_cultura_items_fiestas_nombre: 'Festival of Our Lady of the Assumption',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_fiestas_tag: 'Festivity · León',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_fiestas_descripcion: 'Very popular celebration in León in December. Festival of the Virgin Mary with processions, music, dance, and fireworks.',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_fiestas_detalle: 'La Gritería is a tradition where people shout \'Who causes so much joy?\' and give out gifts.',

paisNicaragua_cultura_items_rubendario_nombre: 'Rubén Darío',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_rubendario_tag: 'Literature · Poetry',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_rubendario_descripcion: 'Nicaragua\'s greatest poet. Father of literary modernism in Spanish.',
paisNicaragua_cultura_items_rubendario_detalle: 'Born in Metapa in 1867. Author of \'Azul\' and \'Cantos de vida y esperanza\'. His tomb is in León Cathedral.',

paisNicaragua_cultura_darkBand_titulo: 'Land of lakes and volcanoes',
paisNicaragua_cultura_darkBand_texto: 'Nicaragua has the largest lake in Central America (Lake Nicaragua, 8,264 km²) and one of the highest concentrations of volcanoes in the region. The country is the birthplace of Rubén Darío, the most influential poet in the Spanish language.',
