// Quick facts
paisBelice_quickFacts_0_titulo: 'Unique in English',
paisBelice_quickFacts_0_texto: 'Belize is the only country in Central America where English is the official language. Spanish, Belizean Creole, Mayan languages (Q\'eqchi\', Mopan, Yucatec), and Garífuna are also spoken.',
paisBelice_quickFacts_1_titulo: 'World-class reefs',
paisBelice_quickFacts_1_texto: 'Its barrier reef is one of the largest and most biodiverse on the planet (Mesoamerican Reef), the second largest in the world after the Australian Great Barrier Reef.',
paisBelice_quickFacts_2_titulo: 'Jungles and Mayan ruins',
paisBelice_quickFacts_2_texto: 'It has tropical rainforest areas with very important Mayan ruins: Caracol (one of the largest Mayan cities), Lamanai, Xunantunich, Altún Ha, and Cahal Pech.',
paisBelice_quickFacts_3_titulo: 'Creole culture',
paisBelice_quickFacts_3_texto: 'Creole-Caribbean identity (Belizean Kriol) is very strong on the coast. Punta rock, brukdown, and paranda are indigenous musical genres.',

// Destinations
paisBelice_destinos_belmopan_nombre: 'Belmopan',
paisBelice_destinos_belmopan_tag: 'Urban · Capital',
paisBelice_destinos_belmopan_descripcion: 'Capital in the interior of Belize. Political and administrative center. Founded in 1970 after Hurricane Hattie.',
paisBelice_destinos_belmopan_detalle: 'Government buildings: National Assembly. Belize Botanical Garden. Nearby caves (St. Herman\'s Cave). Local market. Little tourist activity, quiet city.',
paisBelice_destinos_belmopan_consejo: 'Quick stop, tourism is more on the islands and ruins',

