paisBelice_destinos_sanpedro_descripcion: 'Archipelago of cays, the largest and most popular island in Belize. Very good for diving, snorkeling, and beaches.',
paisBelice_destinos_sanpedro_detalle: 'Blue Hole (famous diving). Hol Chan Marine Reserve (snorkeling with nurse sharks). Secret Beach. Golf cart rides.',
paisBelice_destinos_sanpedro_consejo: 'Book in advance during high season',

paisBelice_destinos_cayocaulker_nombre: 'Caye Caulker',
paisBelice_destinos_cayocaulker_tag: 'Island · Snorkeling · Relax',
paisBelice_destinos_cayocaulker_descripcion: 'Small island with no cars (only golf carts and bicycles). Relaxed atmosphere, ideal for snorkeling, diving, and rest.',
paisBelice_destinos_cayocaulker_detalle: 'The Split (swimming channel). Snorkeling on nearby reefs. Nurse sharks. Overwater restaurants. No cars.',
paisBelice_destinos_cayocaulker_consejo: 'Bring cash, no ATMs on the island',

paisBelice_destinos_xunantunich_nombre: 'Xunantunich',
paisBelice_destinos_xunantunich_tag: 'Archaeology · Maya',
paisBelice_destinos_xunantunich_descripcion: 'Mayan ruins near the Guatemala border. El Castillo (main pyramid) is 40 m high.',
paisBelice_destinos_xunantunich_detalle: 'El Castillo (panoramic views). Stucco frieze on the pyramid. Central Plaza. Access via hand-cranked ferry over the Mopan River.',
paisBelice_destinos_xunantunich_consejo: 'Visit with a local guide',

paisBelice_destinos_caracol_nombre: 'Caracol',
paisBelice_destinos_caracol_tag: 'Archaeology · Maya',
paisBelice_destinos_caracol_descripcion: 'Mayan ruins in western Belize, near the Guatemala border. One of the largest Mayan cities.',
paisBelice_destinos_caracol_detalle: 'Caana (43 m high palace). Acropolis. Ball court. Stelae and monuments.',
paisBelice_destinos_caracol_consejo: 'Difficult access road, recommend 4x4 or tour',

paisBelice_destinos_cockscomb_nombre: 'Cockscomb National Park',
paisBelice_destinos_cockscomb_tag: 'Nature · Jaguars',
paisBelice_destinos_cockscomb_descripcion: 'World\'s first jaguar reserve (declared in 1984). Tropical rainforest with hiking and waterfalls.',
paisBelice_destinos_cockscomb_detalle: 'Jungle hiking. Victoria Peak (1,124 m, Belize\'s highest mountain). Waterfalls (Tiger Fern, Ben\'s Bluff). Jaguar sightings are rare but possible.',
paisBelice_destinos_cockscomb_consejo: 'Excellent for ecotourism, bring repellent',

paisBelice_destinos_lamanai_nombre: 'Lamanai',
paisBelice_destinos_lamanai_tag: 'Archaeology · Maya',
paisBelice_destinos_lamanai_descripcion: 'Mayan ruins with views of the New River. Name means \'submerged crocodile\' in Maya.',
paisBelice_destinos_lamanai_detalle: 'Jaguar and Sun God Mask. Jade Mask Temple. High Temple. Boat ride on the river (crocodile, bird, monkey sightings).',
paisBelice_destinos_lamanai_consejo: 'Tour combining boat ride and walking recommended',

// Culture
paisBelice_cultura_titulo: 'Belizean Culture',
paisBelice_cultura_descripcion: 'Belizean culture blends Maya, Creole (Belizean Kriol), Garífuna, Mestizo, and British influences. English, Creole, Spanish, and Mayan languages coexist in daily life.',
paisBelice_cultura_stats_0_label: 'km²',
paisBelice_cultura_stats_1_label: 'Main languages',
paisBelice_cultura_stats_2_label: 'Independence',
paisBelice_cultura_stats_3_label: 'UNESCO site (Barrier Reef)',

paisBelice_cultura_items_punta_nombre: 'Punta Rock',
paisBelice_cultura_items_punta_tag: 'Music · Garífuna',
paisBelice_cultura_items_punta_descripcion: 'Very popular Garífuna music genre in Belize. Fast rhythm with drums, maracas, and singing.',
paisBelice_cultura_items_punta_detalle: 'Andy Palacio and the Garifuna Collective popularized punta rock internationally. Punta dance involves fast hip movements.',

paisBelice_cultura_items_riceandbeans_nombre: 'Rice and Beans',
paisBelice_cultura_items_riceandbeans_tag: 'Gastronomy',
paisBelice_cultura_items_riceandbeans_descripcion: 'Typical dish with rice and beans cooked in coconut milk. Served with fried chicken or fish.',
paisBelice_cultura_items_riceandbeans_detalle: 'Belizean creole dish: rice and beans cooked in coconut milk, served with stewed chicken or fried fish, coleslaw and ripe plantain.',

paisBelice_cultura_items_garifuna_nombre: 'Garífuna Culture',
paisBelice_cultura_items_garifuna_tag: 'Ethnic group · UNESCO',
paisBelice_cultura_items_garifuna_descripcion: 'Descendants of Africans and Caribs. The Garífuna language was declared a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity (UNESCO).',
paisBelice_cultura_items_garifuna_detalle: 'Main communities in Dangriga, Hopkins, and Punta Gorda. Punta dance, singing, drums.',

paisBelice_cultura_items_chocolate_nombre: 'Belizean Chocolate',
paisBelice_cultura_items_chocolate_tag: 'Gastronomy',
paisBelice_cultura_items_chocolate_descripcion: 'High-quality Belizean cacao. In the south (Toledo) artisanal chocolate is produced.',
paisBelice_cultura_items_chocolate_detalle: 'Chocolate route in Toledo. Artisanal chocolate factories. Mayan cacao has been cultivated since pre-Columbian times.',

paisBelice_cultura_darkBand_titulo: 'Cradle of chocolate and punta rock',
paisBelice_cultura_darkBand_texto: 'Belize is the only Central American country with English as its official language. Garífuna culture (UNESCO) is very strong on the coast. Punta rock is the national music genre.',
paisBelice_cultura_darkBand_datos_0_label: 'British colony',
paisBelice_cultura_darkBand_datos_1_label: 'independence',

// Gastronomy
