paisBelice_aventura_actividades_1_descripcion: 'Marine reserve near Ambergris Caye. Snorkeling with nurse sharks, sea turtles, rays, and tropical fish.',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_2_nombre: 'Cave tubing in Crystal Cave',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_2_descripcion: 'Tube tour through underground rivers inside Mayan caves. Cave systems with stalactite formations.',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_3_nombre: 'Visit to Mayan ruins',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_3_descripcion: 'Caracol (largest Mayan city), Xunantunich (El Castillo), Lamanai (boat access), Altún Ha (near Belize City).',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_4_nombre: 'Hiking in Cockscomb Jaguar Reserve',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_4_descripcion: 'World\'s first jaguar reserve. Trails to waterfalls (Tiger Fern) and Victoria Peak (1,124 m).',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_5_nombre: 'Beach tourism on the cays',
paisBelice_aventura_actividades_5_descripcion: 'Ambergris Caye (diving), Caye Caulker (relax, car-free), Ambergris Caye. Beaches, sun, and Caribbean sea.',

paisBelice_aventura_darkBand_titulo: 'Second largest coral barrier in the world',
paisBelice_aventura_darkBand_texto: 'Belize has the second largest coral reef on the planet (Mesoamerican Reef), after the Australian Great Barrier Reef. It is the only Central American country with English as its official language.',
